  "description": "`connection_record.login` (OPEN-R2 (a)): where the connection's login came from, the value `session.connect`'s `detail.login` takes for it. `credential_ref` stays the constant `supplied` for a supplied or a prompted login and `login` tells them apart, so a prompted connection stays reusable by its principal across a restart and a rebuilt `session.connect` says `prompted`. Placement: `supplied` and `prompted` only beside `credential_ref` `supplied`; `stored` only beside another reference. A core of this release writes it on every SSH connection record and never on a telnet or echo one; an absent value reads as `credential_ref` says (`supplied` for the constant, otherwise `stored` on an SSH connection), so every older record keeps its meaning. Valid: the three values in their places; absent. Invalid: each out of place.",
  "corpus": [
    "Contract §15.3",
    "open_decisions §5",
    "device-login, reusing a prompted connection",
    "session-open step 18"
  ],
